    description: "Add a safety check to `scripts/bakeoff-deep init` (and bakeoff-broad) that detects when a recent session (< 7 days) exists with the same code hash and would be a candidate for iteration instead of a new session. Print a warning suggesting the user run `cycle` against the existing session instead. Should be opt-out (warning + 5s sleep), not blocking. Per playbook clarification commit (deep-iteration-vs-new-session). User explicitly approved deferring this as a tracker item."  # 9ddc
